1
00:00:01,850 --> 00:00:09,110
Chapter 37 The man a house of Fondin was a building of considerable antiquity,

2
00:00:09,630 --> 00:00:14,929
moderate size, and no architectural pretensions, deep buried in a wood.

3
00:00:15,690 --> 00:00:16,970
I had heard of it before.

4
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:21,350
Mr. Rochester often spoke of it, and sometimes went there.

5
00:00:22,429 --> 00:00:25,949
His father had purchased the estate for the sake of the game covers.

6
00:00:27,089 --> 00:00:30,533
He would have let the house, but could find no tenant,

7
00:00:30,535 --> 00:00:34,570
in consequence of its ineligible and in salubrious sight.

8
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:40,669
Fondin then remained uninhabited and unfurnished, with the exception of some

9
00:00:40,671 --> 00:00:43,887
two or three rooms fitted up for the accommodation of

10
00:00:43,888 --> 00:00:46,789
the Squire, when he went there in the season to shoot.

11
00:00:48,050 --> 00:00:53,630
To this house I came just air-dark, on an evening marked by the

12
00:00:53,630 --> 00:01:00,070
characteristics of Sad Sky, cold gale, and continued small penetrating rain.

13
00:01:01,350 --> 00:01:06,429
The last mile I performed on foot, having dismissed the shades and driver

14
00:01:06,430 --> 00:01:10,316
with the double remuneration I had promised engineed,

15
00:01:10,316 --> 00:01:13,250
even when within a very short distance of the man-house.

16
00:01:14,289 --> 00:01:17,415
You could see nothing of it, so thick and dark

17
00:01:17,417 --> 00:01:20,951
grew the timber of the gloomy wood about it.

18
00:01:21,649 --> 00:01:27,130
Iron gates between granite pillars showed me where to enter, and passing through

19
00:01:27,130 --> 00:01:32,949
them, I found myself at once in the twilight of close-ranked trees.

20
00:01:33,949 --> 00:01:37,259
There was a grass-grown track descending the forest aisle

21
00:01:37,259 --> 00:01:41,110
between whore and naughty shafts and underbranched arches.

22
00:01:41,111 --> 00:01:48,029
I followed it, expecting soon to reach the dwelling, but it stretched on and on.

23
00:01:48,750 --> 00:01:50,550
It wound far and farther.

24
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:53,970
No sign of habitation or grounds was visible.

25
00:01:54,830 --> 00:01:58,050
I thought I had taken a wrong direction and lost my way.

26
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:02,970
The darkness of natural as well as of silver and dusk gathered over me.

27
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:05,929
I looked round in search of another road.

28
00:02:06,649 --> 00:02:07,649
There was none.

29
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:14,130
All was interwoven stem, column a trunk, dense summer foliage, no opening anywhere.

30
00:02:15,289 --> 00:02:16,470
I proceeded.

31
00:02:17,029 --> 00:02:20,389
At last my way opened, the trees thinned a little.

32
00:02:21,089 --> 00:02:26,250
Presently I beheld a railing, then the house, scarce by this dim light,

33
00:02:26,770 --> 00:02:32,251
distinguishable from the trees, so dank and green where it's decaying walls.

34
00:02:32,910 --> 00:02:38,889
Entering a portal, fastened only by a latch, I stood amidst a space of enclosed

35
00:02:38,891 --> 00:02:42,630
ground from which the woods swept away in a semicircle.

36
00:02:43,649 --> 00:02:49,610
There were no flowers, no garden beds, only a broad gravel walk girdling a grass

37
00:02:49,611 --> 00:02:53,570
-plat, and this set in the heavy frame of the forest.

38
00:02:54,830 --> 00:02:57,850
The house presented two pointed gables in its front.

39
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:00,449
The windows were lattice and narrow.

40
00:03:01,229 --> 00:03:02,750
The front door was narrow too.

41
00:03:03,570 --> 00:03:05,029
One step led up to it.

42
00:03:05,910 --> 00:03:12,191
The whole looked as the host of the Rochester arms had said, quite a desolate spot.

43
00:03:12,669 --> 00:03:14,830
It was as still as a church on a weekday.

44
00:03:15,770 --> 00:03:21,091
The patterning rain on the forest leaves was the only sound audible in its vicinage.

45
00:03:21,570 --> 00:03:23,130
Can there be life here?

46
00:03:23,630 --> 00:03:24,630
I asked.

47
00:03:24,970 --> 00:03:31,050
Yes, life of some kind there was, for I heard a movement, that narrow front

48
00:03:31,051 --> 00:03:35,970
door was unclosing, and some shape was about to issue from the grainage.

49
00:03:36,570 --> 00:03:37,990
It opened slowly.

50
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:42,970
A figure came out into the twilight and stood on the step, a man without a hat.

51
00:03:43,789 --> 00:03:46,729
He stretched forth his hand as if to feel whether it rained.

52
00:03:47,710 --> 00:03:50,990
Dusk as it was, I had recognized him.

53
00:03:51,710 --> 00:03:55,830
It was my master, Edward Fairfax Rochester, and no other.

54
00:03:56,369 --> 00:04:02,270
I stayed my step, almost my breath, and stood to watch him, to examine him,

55
00:04:02,809 --> 00:04:06,130
myself unseen and alas, to him invisible.

56
00:04:07,050 --> 00:04:11,610
It was a sudden meeting, and one in which rapture was kept well in check by pain.

57
00:04:12,990 --> 00:04:16,077
I had no difficulty in restraining my voice

58
00:04:16,077 --> 00:04:19,930
from exclamation, my step from hasty advance.

59
00:04:20,589 --> 00:04:24,490
His form was of the same strong and stalwart contour as ever.

60
00:04:24,770 --> 00:04:28,725
His port was still erect, his hair was still raven

61
00:04:28,726 --> 00:04:32,210
black, nor were his features altered or sunk.

62
00:04:32,970 --> 00:04:36,990
Not in one year's space, by any sorrow, could his athletic

63
00:04:36,991 --> 00:04:40,589
strength be quelled or his vigorous prime blighted.

64
00:04:42,009 --> 00:04:47,850
But in his countenance, I saw a change, that looked desperate and brooding.

65
00:04:48,649 --> 00:04:51,918
That reminded me of some wronged and fettered wild

66
00:04:51,918 --> 00:04:55,649
beast or bird, dangerous to approach in his sullen woe.

67
00:04:56,210 --> 00:05:00,263
The caged eagle, whose gold ring dies cruelty has

68
00:05:00,263 --> 00:05:04,029
extinguished, might look as looked that sightless Samson.

69
00:05:05,029 --> 00:05:09,190
And Rida, do you think I feared him in his blind ferocity?

70
00:05:10,130 --> 00:05:12,089
If you do, you little know me.

71
00:05:12,869 --> 00:05:16,203
A soft hope, blent with my sorrow that soon, I

72
00:05:16,205 --> 00:05:19,691
should dare to drop a kiss on that brow of rock.

73
00:05:20,350 --> 00:05:23,543
And on these lips so sternly sealed beneath

74
00:05:23,543 --> 00:05:26,570
it, but not yet, I would not accost him yet.

75
00:05:27,369 --> 00:05:34,410
He descended the one step and advanced slowly and gropingly towards the grass -plat.

76
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:36,529
Where was his daring stride now?

77
00:05:37,449 --> 00:05:40,710
Then he paused, as if he knew not which way to turn.

78
00:05:41,429 --> 00:05:47,929
He lifted his hand and opened his eyelids, gazed blank and with a straining effort on

79
00:05:47,930 --> 00:05:50,809
the sky and toward the amphitheater of trees.

80
00:05:52,089 --> 00:05:54,889
One saw that all to him was void darkness.

81
00:05:56,149 --> 00:05:58,899
He stretched his right hand, the left arm, the

82
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:02,471
mutilated one, he kept hidden in his bosom.

83
00:06:02,729 --> 00:06:06,929
He seemed to wish by touch to gain an idea of what lay around him.

84
00:06:07,550 --> 00:06:12,830
He met but vacancy still, for the trees were some yards off where he stood.

85
00:06:13,789 --> 00:06:19,889
He relinquished the endeavor, folded his arms, and stood quiet and mute in the

86
00:06:19,891 --> 00:06:23,490
rain, now falling fast on his uncovered head.

87
00:06:24,669 --> 00:06:28,990
At this moment John approached him from some quarter.

88
00:06:30,610 --> 00:06:33,009
Will you take my arm, sir, he said.

89
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:35,889
There is a heavy shower coming on.

90
00:06:36,350 --> 00:06:37,410
Had you not better go in?

91
00:06:38,869 --> 00:06:40,830
Let me alone was the answer.

92
00:06:41,889 --> 00:06:44,029
John withdrew without having observed me.

93
00:06:45,009 --> 00:06:48,009
Mr. Rochester now tried to walk about, vainly.

94
00:06:48,669 --> 00:06:49,850
All was too uncertain.

95
00:06:50,830 --> 00:06:55,130
He groped his way back to the house and re -entering it, closed the door.

96
00:06:55,809 --> 00:06:57,789
I now drew near and knocked.

97
00:06:58,570 --> 00:06:59,929
John's wife opened for me.

98
00:07:01,110 --> 00:07:03,350
Mary, I said, how are you?

99
00:07:04,330 --> 00:07:06,789
She started as if she had seen a ghost.

100
00:07:07,389 --> 00:07:08,389
I calmed her.

101
00:07:09,050 --> 00:07:15,010
To her hurried, is it really you, miss, come at this late hour to this lonely place?

102
00:07:15,770 --> 00:07:20,270
I answered by taking her hand, and then I followed her into the kitchen,

103
00:07:21,009 --> 00:07:23,509
where John now sat by a good fire.

104
00:07:24,449 --> 00:07:30,509
I explained to them in few words that I had heard all which had happened since I

105
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:34,710
left Thornfield, and that I was come to see Mr. Rochester.

106
00:07:35,889 --> 00:07:41,089
I asked John to go down to the turnpike house, where I had dismissed the shades

107
00:07:41,091 --> 00:07:44,449
and bring my trunk, which I had left there.

108
00:07:45,429 --> 00:07:52,050
And then, while I removed my bonnet and shawl, I questioned Mary as to whether I

109
00:07:52,051 --> 00:07:56,990
could be accommodated at the manor house for the night, and finding that

110
00:07:56,990 --> 00:08:01,369
arrangements to that effect, though difficult would not be impossible,

111
00:08:02,029 --> 00:08:04,449
I informed her I should stay.

112
00:08:05,429 --> 00:08:08,809
Just at this moment, the parlor bell rang.

113
00:08:09,789 --> 00:08:13,767
When you go in, said I, tell your master that a

114
00:08:13,769 --> 00:08:17,369
person wishes to speak to him but do not give my name.

115
00:08:18,889 --> 00:08:21,110
I don't think he will see you, she answered.

116
00:08:21,809 --> 00:08:23,190
He refuses everybody.

117
00:08:24,169 --> 00:08:27,190
When she returned, I inquired what he had said.

118
00:08:28,309 --> 00:08:31,610
You are to send in your name and your business, she replied.

119
00:08:33,509 --> 00:08:36,180
She then proceeded to fill a glass with water

120
00:08:36,182 --> 00:08:39,650
and place it on a tray together with candles.

121
00:08:40,350 --> 00:08:41,690
Is that what he rang for?

122
00:08:41,691 --> 00:08:42,691
I asked.

123
00:08:42,970 --> 00:08:47,869
Yes, he always has candles brought in at dark, though he is blind.

124
00:08:49,130 --> 00:08:51,289
Give the tray to me, I will carry it in.

125
00:08:52,350 --> 00:08:55,490
I took it from her hand, she pointed me out the parlor door.

126
00:08:56,809 --> 00:08:58,729
The tray shook as I held it.

127
00:08:59,369 --> 00:09:00,889
The water spilt from the glass.

128
00:09:01,910 --> 00:09:05,066
My heart struck my ribs loud and fast, Mary

129
00:09:05,066 --> 00:09:08,710
opened the door for me and shut it behind me.

130
00:09:09,669 --> 00:09:11,410
This parlor looked gloomy.

131
00:09:11,690 --> 00:09:14,970
A neglected handful of fire burnt low in the grate.

132
00:09:15,850 --> 00:09:20,570
And leaning over it, with his head supported against the high old-fashioned

133
00:09:20,570 --> 00:09:24,449
mantelpiece, appeared the blind tenant of the room.

134
00:09:25,729 --> 00:09:32,429
His old dog, Pilate, lay on one side, removed out of the way, and coiled up as

135
00:09:32,430 --> 00:09:35,210
if afraid of being inadvertently trodden upon.

136
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:39,169
Pilate pricked up his ears when I came in.

137
00:09:40,089 --> 00:09:43,889
Then he jumped up with a help and a whine and bounded towards me.

138
00:09:44,630 --> 00:09:46,529
He almost knocked the tray from my hands.

139
00:09:47,110 --> 00:09:50,550
I set it on the table, then patted him and said softly.

140
00:09:51,970 --> 00:09:52,970
Lie down.

141
00:09:54,029 --> 00:09:57,351
Mr. Rochester turned mechanically to see what the commotion

142
00:09:57,353 --> 00:10:01,210
was, but as he saw nothing, he returned and sighed.

143
00:10:02,089 --> 00:10:04,570
Give me the water, Mary, he said.

144
00:10:05,190 --> 00:10:08,410
I approached him, with the now only half -filled glass.

145
00:10:09,050 --> 00:10:10,809
Pilate followed me, still excited.

146
00:10:11,589 --> 00:10:13,470
What is the matter, he inquired?

147
00:10:14,289 --> 00:10:16,070
Down Pilate, I again said.

148
00:10:16,929 --> 00:10:20,130
He checked the water on its way to his lips, and seemed to listen.

149
00:10:21,210 --> 00:10:23,009
He drank and put the glass down.

150
00:10:24,470 --> 00:10:26,309
This is you, Mary, is it not?

151
00:10:27,850 --> 00:10:29,770
Mary is in the kitchen, I answered.

152
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:34,610
He put out his hand with a quick gesture, but not seeing where I stood.

153
00:10:35,270 --> 00:10:36,330
He did not touch me.

154
00:10:37,330 --> 00:10:38,330
Who is this?

155
00:10:38,910 --> 00:10:39,910
Who is this?

156
00:10:40,270 --> 00:10:44,086
He demanded, trying as it seemed to see with those

157
00:10:44,088 --> 00:10:47,389
cyclist's eyes, unavailing and distressing attempt.

158
00:10:48,130 --> 00:10:48,649
Answer me.

159
00:10:48,949 --> 00:10:52,690
Speak again, he ordered, empiriously and allowed.

160
00:10:53,809 --> 00:10:55,330
Will you have a little more water, sir?

161
00:10:55,970 --> 00:10:58,630
I spilt half of what was in the glass, I said.

162
00:10:59,910 --> 00:11:00,910
Who is it?

163
00:11:00,970 --> 00:11:01,490
What is it?

164
00:11:01,869 --> 00:11:02,869
Who speaks?

165
00:11:03,949 --> 00:11:07,169
Pilate knows me, and John and Mary know I am here.

166
00:11:07,929 --> 00:11:10,070
I came only this evening, I answered.

167
00:11:10,929 --> 00:11:11,929
Great God!

168
00:11:12,610 --> 00:11:14,070
What delusion has come over me.

169
00:11:14,770 --> 00:11:16,869
What sweet madness has seized me?

170
00:11:18,130 --> 00:11:19,130
No delusion.

171
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:20,550
No madness.

172
00:11:20,789 --> 00:11:23,449
Your mind, sir, is too strong for delusion.

173
00:11:23,949 --> 00:11:25,669
Your health too sound for frenzy.

174
00:11:26,429 --> 00:11:27,429
And where is the speaker?

175
00:11:28,130 --> 00:11:29,130
Is it only a voice?

176
00:11:29,830 --> 00:11:35,250
Oh, I cannot see, but I must feel, or my heart will stop and my brain burst.

177
00:11:36,110 --> 00:11:40,330
Whatever, whoever you are, be perceptible to the touch, or I cannot live.

178
00:11:41,130 --> 00:11:42,229
He groped.

179
00:11:42,690 --> 00:11:46,550
I arrested his wandering hand and prisoned it in both mine.

180
00:11:47,809 --> 00:11:50,029
Her very fingers, he cried.

181
00:11:50,529 --> 00:11:54,130
Her small slight fingers, if so there must be more of her.

182
00:11:54,910 --> 00:11:57,130
The muscular hand broke from my custody.

183
00:11:57,889 --> 00:12:00,490
My arm was seized, my shoulder, neck, waist.

184
00:12:01,309 --> 00:12:03,190
I was entwined and gathered to him.

185
00:12:04,669 --> 00:12:05,669
Is it Jane?

186
00:12:06,190 --> 00:12:07,190
What is it?

187
00:12:07,410 --> 00:12:08,410
This is her shape.

188
00:12:08,850 --> 00:12:09,850
This is her size.

189
00:12:10,509 --> 00:12:12,309
And this her voice, I added.

190
00:12:13,009 --> 00:12:14,009
She is all here.

191
00:12:14,229 --> 00:12:15,229
Her heart too.

192
00:12:15,809 --> 00:12:16,809
God bless you, sir.

193
00:12:17,490 --> 00:12:19,050
I am glad to be so near you again.

194
00:12:20,270 --> 00:12:23,369
Jane heir, Jane heir, was all he said.

195
00:12:24,710 --> 00:12:26,550
My dear master, I answered.

196
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:28,330
I am Jane heir.

197
00:12:28,710 --> 00:12:29,710
I have found you out.

198
00:12:29,789 --> 00:12:30,850
I am come back to you.

199
00:12:31,990 --> 00:12:32,990
In truth?

200
00:12:33,330 --> 00:12:34,330
In the flesh?

201
00:12:34,589 --> 00:12:35,589
My living Jane?

202
00:12:36,490 --> 00:12:37,490
You touch me, sir.

203
00:12:37,830 --> 00:12:39,570
You hold me and fast enough.

204
00:12:40,210 --> 00:12:43,589
I am not cold like a corpse, nor vacant like air, am I?

205
00:12:44,770 --> 00:12:49,369
My living darling, these are certainly her limbs and these her features.

206
00:12:50,429 --> 00:12:53,509
But I cannot be so blessed after all my misery.

207
00:12:54,490 --> 00:12:55,490
It is a dream.

208
00:12:56,429 --> 00:13:01,610
Such dreams as I have had at night when I have clasped her once more to my heart as

209
00:13:01,611 --> 00:13:06,195
I do now and kissed her as thus and felt that she

210
00:13:06,197 --> 00:13:09,591
loved me and trusted that she would not leave me.

211
00:13:10,809 --> 00:13:14,169
Which I never will, sir, from this day.

212
00:13:15,389 --> 00:13:17,770
And never will, says the vision.

213
00:13:18,669 --> 00:13:23,830
But I always woken found it in empty mockery and I was desolate and abandoned.

214
00:13:24,550 --> 00:13:29,750
My life dark, lonely, hopeless, my soul a thirst and forbidden to drink.

215
00:13:30,570 --> 00:13:36,750
My heart famished and never to be fed, gentle, soft dream, nestling in my arms

216
00:13:36,751 --> 00:13:40,440
now, you will fly too, as your sisters have all fled

217
00:13:40,441 --> 00:13:43,949
before you, but kiss me before you go, embrace me, Jane.

218
00:13:45,610 --> 00:13:47,649
There, sir, and there.

219
00:13:48,529 --> 00:13:51,990
I pressed my lips to his once brilliant and now rayless eyes.

220
00:13:52,770 --> 00:13:55,149
I swept his hair from his brow and kissed that too.

221
00:13:56,429 --> 00:13:58,449
He suddenly seemed to arouse himself.

222
00:13:59,110 --> 00:14:02,029
The conviction of the reality of all this seized him.

223
00:14:03,089 --> 00:14:04,089
It is you.

224
00:14:04,270 --> 00:14:05,270
Is it Jane?

225
00:14:05,490 --> 00:14:06,690
You will come back to me then.

226
00:14:07,990 --> 00:14:08,990
I am.

227
00:14:09,490 --> 00:14:12,369
And you do not lie dead in some ditch under some stream.

228
00:14:13,330 --> 00:14:15,449
And you are not a pining outcast among strangers.

229
00:14:16,550 --> 00:14:19,250
No, sir, I am an independent woman now.

230
00:14:20,009 --> 00:14:20,289
Independent.

231
00:14:20,850 --> 00:14:21,850
What do you mean, Jane?

232
00:14:23,130 --> 00:14:24,990
My uncle in Madera is dead.

233
00:14:25,690 --> 00:14:27,889
And he left me five thousand pounds.

234
00:14:28,869 --> 00:14:30,389
Ah, this is practical.

235
00:14:30,809 --> 00:14:32,009
This is real, he cried.

236
00:14:32,669 --> 00:14:33,710
I should never dream that.

237
00:14:34,369 --> 00:14:39,470
Besides, there is that peculiar voice of hers, so animating and pequon,

238
00:14:39,970 --> 00:14:40,970
as well as soft.

239
00:14:41,350 --> 00:14:42,529
It cheers my withered heart.

240
00:14:43,229 --> 00:14:44,550
It puts life into it.

241
00:14:45,389 --> 00:14:46,389
What, Janet?

242
00:14:46,949 --> 00:14:48,229
Are you an independent woman?

243
00:14:48,789 --> 00:14:49,789
A rich woman.

244
00:14:51,509 --> 00:14:52,690
Quite rich, sir.

245
00:14:53,410 --> 00:14:55,334
If you won't let me live with you, I can

246
00:14:55,335 --> 00:14:57,410
build a house of my own close-up to your door.

247
00:14:57,929 --> 00:15:01,149
And you may come and sit in my parlour when you want company of an evening.

248
00:15:03,050 --> 00:15:09,830
But as you are rich, Jane, you have now no doubt, friends who will look after you,

249
00:15:10,550 --> 00:15:14,449
and not suffer you to devote yourself to a blind lambator like me.

250
00:15:15,830 --> 00:15:18,770
I told you I'm independent, sir, as well as rich.

251
00:15:19,389 --> 00:15:20,389
I am my own mistress.

252
00:15:22,250 --> 00:15:25,910
And you will stay with me, certainly, unless you object.

253
00:15:26,970 --> 00:15:30,449
I will be your neighbour, your nurse, your housekeeper.

254
00:15:31,529 --> 00:15:32,809
I find you lonely.

255
00:15:33,809 --> 00:15:38,210
I will be your companion to read to you, to walk with you, to sit with you,

256
00:15:38,330 --> 00:15:40,529
to wait on you, to be eyes and hands to you.

257
00:15:41,429 --> 00:15:43,850
Seize to look so melancholy, my dear master.

258
00:15:44,690 --> 00:15:47,070
You shall not be left desolate, so long as I live.

259
00:15:48,289 --> 00:15:49,570
He replied not.

260
00:15:50,550 --> 00:15:52,929
He seemed serious, abstracted.

261
00:15:53,490 --> 00:15:54,490
He sighed.

262
00:15:54,850 --> 00:15:57,210
He half-opened his lips as if to speak.

263
00:15:58,169 --> 00:15:59,169
He closed them again.

264
00:16:00,149 --> 00:16:01,570
I felt a little embarrassed.

265
00:16:02,550 --> 00:16:07,970
Perhaps I had too rashly over-leaped conventionalities, and he, like Sinjin,

266
00:16:08,750 --> 00:16:11,449
saw impropriety in my inconsiderateness.

267
00:16:12,229 --> 00:16:15,032
I had indeed made my proposal from the idea

268
00:16:15,033 --> 00:16:18,710
that he wished and would ask me to be his wife.

269
00:16:19,210 --> 00:16:25,250
An expectation, not the less certain, because unexpressed, had buoyed me up,

270
00:16:25,690 --> 00:16:27,949
that he would claim me at once as his own.

271
00:16:29,789 --> 00:16:36,270
But no hint to that effect, escaping him and his countenance becoming more overcast.

272
00:16:36,509 --> 00:16:41,529
I suddenly remembered that I might have been all wrong, and was perhaps playing

273
00:16:41,531 --> 00:16:45,241
the fool unwittingly, and I began gently to withdraw

274
00:16:45,243 --> 00:16:49,570
myself from his arms, but he eagerly snatched me closer.

275
00:16:50,669 --> 00:16:53,070
No, no, Jane, you must not go.

276
00:16:53,570 --> 00:16:58,210
No, I have touched you, heard you, felt the comfort of your presence,

277
00:16:58,949 --> 00:17:00,809
the sweetness of your consolation.

278
00:17:01,550 --> 00:17:03,250
I cannot give up these joys.

279
00:17:03,649 --> 00:17:05,190
I have little left in myself.

280
00:17:05,550 --> 00:17:06,570
I must have you.

281
00:17:07,369 --> 00:17:12,669
The world may laugh, may call me absurd, selfish, but it does not signify.

282
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:14,830
My very soul demands you.

283
00:17:15,289 --> 00:17:19,389
It will be satisfied, or it will take deadly vengeance on its frame.

284
00:17:21,229 --> 00:17:23,429
Well, sir, I will stay with you.

285
00:17:23,850 --> 00:17:24,850
I have said so.

286
00:17:26,229 --> 00:17:32,130
Yes, but you understand one thing by staying with me, and I understand another.

287
00:17:33,289 --> 00:17:38,250
You, perhaps, could make up your mind to be about my hand and chair.

288
00:17:39,289 --> 00:17:45,270
To wait on me as a kind little nurse, for you have an affectionate heart and a

289
00:17:45,270 --> 00:17:49,729
generous spirit which prompts you to make sacrifices for those you pity.

290
00:17:50,669 --> 00:17:53,190
And that ought to suffice for me no doubt.

291
00:17:54,009 --> 00:17:58,169
I suppose I should now entertain none but fatherly feelings for you.

292
00:17:58,789 --> 00:17:59,309
Do you think so?

293
00:17:59,729 --> 00:18:00,770
Come, tell me.

294
00:18:02,130 --> 00:18:04,070
I will think what you like, sir.

295
00:18:04,809 --> 00:18:09,429
I am content to be only your nurse if you think it better.

296
00:18:10,889 --> 00:18:13,190
But you cannot always be my nurse, Janet.

297
00:18:13,809 --> 00:18:14,809
You are young.

298
00:18:15,490 --> 00:18:16,889
You must marry one day.

299
00:18:17,949 --> 00:18:19,270
I don't care about being married.

300
00:18:20,229 --> 00:18:21,229
You should care, Janet.

301
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:24,889
If I were what I once was, I would try to make you care.

302
00:18:25,789 --> 00:18:27,389
But a sightless block.

303
00:18:28,710 --> 00:18:30,750
He relapsed again into gloom.

304
00:18:31,630 --> 00:18:36,149
I, on the contrary, became more cheerful and took fresh courage.

305
00:18:37,210 --> 00:18:41,470
These last words gave me an insight as to where the difficulty lay.

306
00:18:42,330 --> 00:18:44,869
And as it was no difficulty with me, I felt

307
00:18:44,870 --> 00:18:47,790
quite relieved from my previous embarrassment.

308
00:18:48,149 --> 00:18:50,869
I resumed a lively vein of conversation.

309
00:18:52,470 --> 00:18:56,417
It is time someone undertook to rehumanize you,

310
00:18:56,418 --> 00:19:00,570
said I, parting his thick and long uncut locks.

311
00:19:01,429 --> 00:19:06,389
For I see you are being metamorphosed into a lion, or something of that sort.

312
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:13,169
You have a four air of Nebuchadnezzar in the fields about you, that is certain.

313
00:19:14,210 --> 00:19:16,330
Your hair reminds me of eagle's feathers.

314
00:19:17,330 --> 00:19:22,309
Whether your nails are grown like birds claws or not, I have not yet noticed.

315
00:19:23,770 --> 00:19:27,070
On this arm, I have neither hand nor nails.

316
00:19:27,929 --> 00:19:32,949
He said, drawing the mutilated limb from his breast and showing it to me.

317
00:19:33,910 --> 00:19:36,649
It is a mere stump, a ghastly sight.

318
00:19:37,470 --> 00:19:38,470
Don't you think so, Jane?

319
00:19:39,649 --> 00:19:46,669
It is a pity to see it, and a pity to see your eyes, and the scar of fire on your

320
00:19:46,671 --> 00:19:50,876
forehead, and the worst of it is, one is in danger of

321
00:19:50,876 --> 00:19:55,490
loving you too well for all this and making too much of you.

322
00:19:56,550 --> 00:20:03,270
I thought you would be revolted, Jane, when you saw my arm and my cicatrized visage.

323
00:20:04,009 --> 00:20:11,051
Did you, don't tell me so, lest I should say something disparaging to your judgment?

324
00:20:11,729 --> 00:20:18,149
Now, let me leave you an instant to make a better fire and have the hearth swept up.

325
00:20:18,809 --> 00:20:20,369
Can you tell when there is a good fire?

326
00:20:21,169 --> 00:20:26,750
Yes, with the right eye I see a glow, a ruddy haze, and you see the candles.

327
00:20:27,850 --> 00:20:30,270
Very dimly, each is a luminous cloud.

328
00:20:31,250 --> 00:20:32,250
Can you see me?

329
00:20:33,270 --> 00:20:37,610
No, my fairy, but I am only too thankful to hear and feel you.

330
00:20:38,210 --> 00:20:39,449
When do you take supper?

331
00:20:40,190 --> 00:20:43,690
I never take supper, but you shall have some tonight.

332
00:20:44,210 --> 00:20:47,910
I am hungry, so are you, I dare say, only you forget.

333
00:20:49,630 --> 00:20:53,490
Summoning Mary, I soon had the room in more cheerful order.

334
00:20:54,289 --> 00:20:58,130
I prepared him, likewise, a comfortable repast.

335
00:20:58,850 --> 00:21:04,190
My spirits were excited, and with pleasure and ease I talked to him during supper,

336
00:21:04,929 --> 00:21:06,130
and for a long time after.

337
00:21:07,369 --> 00:21:12,949
There was no harassing restraint, no repressing of glee and vivacity with him.

338
00:21:13,729 --> 00:21:18,589
For with him I was at perfect ease, because I knew I suited him.

339
00:21:19,550 --> 00:21:25,610
All I said or did seemed either to console or revive him, delightful consciousness.

340
00:21:25,611 --> 00:21:28,910
It brought to life and light my whole nature.

341
00:21:29,789 --> 00:21:33,470
In his presence I thoroughly lived, and he lived in mine.

342
00:21:34,490 --> 00:21:39,929
Blind as he was, smiles played over his face, joy dawned on his forehead,

343
00:21:40,610 --> 00:21:43,070
his lineaments softened and warmed.

344
00:21:44,429 --> 00:21:48,669
After supper he began to ask me many questions of where I had been,

345
00:21:49,070 --> 00:21:51,721
what I had been doing, how I had found him

346
00:21:51,722 --> 00:21:55,391
out, but I gave him only very partial replies.

347
00:21:56,089 --> 00:21:59,050
It was too late to enter into particulars that night.

348
00:22:00,070 --> 00:22:04,487
Besides, I wished to touch no deep thrilling cord,

349
00:22:04,489 --> 00:22:07,369
to open no fresh well of emotion in his heart.

350
00:22:08,229 --> 00:22:10,490
My sole present aim was to cheer him.

351
00:22:11,289 --> 00:22:15,509
Cheered, as I have said, he was, and yet but by fits.

352
00:22:16,389 --> 00:22:19,669
If a moment silence broke the conversation, he would turn restless,

353
00:22:20,350 --> 00:22:26,070
touch me, then say, Jane, you are altogether a human being, Jane.

354
00:22:26,889 --> 00:22:27,949
You are certain of that?

355
00:22:29,309 --> 00:22:35,850
I conscientiously believe so, Mr. Rochester, yet how, on this dark and

356
00:22:35,850 --> 00:22:40,029
doleful evening, could you so suddenly rise on my lone heart?

357
00:22:41,470 --> 00:22:43,963
I stretched my hand to take a glass of water

358
00:22:43,964 --> 00:22:47,270
from a hiling, and it was given me by you.

359
00:22:47,789 --> 00:22:54,309
I asked a question, expecting John's wife to answer me, and your voice spoke at my

360
00:22:54,311 --> 00:22:59,250
ear, because I had come in in Mary's stead with the tray.

361
00:23:00,130 --> 00:23:04,470
And there is enchantment in the very hour I am now spending with you.

362
00:23:06,449 --> 00:23:11,490
Who can tell what a dark, dreary, hopeless life I have dragged on for months

363
00:23:11,490 --> 00:23:18,690
past, doing nothing, expecting nothing, merging night in day, feeling but the

364
00:23:18,691 --> 00:23:23,149
sensation of cold when I let the fire go out, of hunger when I forgot to eat,

365
00:23:23,910 --> 00:23:27,461
and then a ceaseless sorrow, and at times a

366
00:23:27,463 --> 00:23:31,471
very delirium of desire to behold my Jane again.

367
00:23:32,190 --> 00:23:37,449
Yes, for her restoration I longed far more than for that of my lost sight.

368
00:23:39,429 --> 00:23:42,889
How can it be that Jane is with me, and says she loves me?

369
00:23:43,770 --> 00:23:45,869
Will she not depart as suddenly as she came?

370
00:23:46,529 --> 00:23:48,889
Tomorrow I fear I shall find her no more.

371
00:23:50,190 --> 00:23:54,669
A commonplace, practical reply, out of the train of his own disturbed

372
00:23:54,671 --> 00:24:01,589
ideas, was I was sure the best and most reassuring for him in this frame of mind.

373
00:24:02,750 --> 00:24:07,529
I passed my finger over his eyebrows, and remarked that they were scorched,

374
00:24:08,149 --> 00:24:10,592
and that I would apply something which would

375
00:24:10,593 --> 00:24:14,091
make them grow as broad and black as ever.

376
00:24:15,389 --> 00:24:21,070
Where is the use of doing me good in any way beneficent spirit when, at some fatal

377
00:24:21,070 --> 00:24:26,770
moment, you will again desert me, passing like a shadow, wither and how to

378
00:24:26,770 --> 00:24:30,690
me unknown, and for me remaining afterwards undiscoverable.

379
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:33,729
Have your pocket come about you, sir?

380
00:24:34,869 --> 00:24:35,869
What for, Jane?

381
00:24:36,770 --> 00:24:38,729
Just to comb out this shaggy black mane.

382
00:24:39,869 --> 00:24:42,830
I find you rather alarming when I examine you close at hand.

383
00:24:43,429 --> 00:24:47,990
You talk of my being a fairy, but I am sure you are more like a brownie.

384
00:24:49,149 --> 00:24:50,429
Am I hideous, Jane?

385
00:24:51,509 --> 00:24:53,550
Very sir, you always were, you know?

386
00:24:55,009 --> 00:25:00,050
The wickedness has not been taken out of you wherever you have sojourned.

387
00:25:00,869 --> 00:25:06,270
Yet I have been with good people, far better than you, a hundred times

388
00:25:06,270 --> 00:25:11,429
better people, possessed of ideas and views you never entertained in your life.

389
00:25:12,550 --> 00:25:14,690
Quite more refined and exalted.

390
00:25:15,990 --> 00:25:17,649
Who the doose have you been with?

391
00:25:18,710 --> 00:25:22,130
If you twist in that way, you will make me pull the hair out of your head.

392
00:25:22,850 --> 00:25:27,410
And then I think you will cease to entertain doubts of my substantiality.

393
00:25:29,050 --> 00:25:30,669
Who have you been with, Jane?

394
00:25:32,529 --> 00:25:35,009
You shall not get it out of me tonight, sir.

395
00:25:35,809 --> 00:25:41,529
You must wait till tomorrow, to leave my tale half told, will, you know,

396
00:25:42,089 --> 00:25:46,029
be a sort of security that I shall appear at your breakfast table to finish it.

397
00:25:47,389 --> 00:25:53,529
By the by, I must mind not to rise on your hearth with only a glass of water then.

398
00:25:54,410 --> 00:25:58,229
I must bring an egg at the least to say nothing of fried ham.

399
00:26:00,029 --> 00:26:03,801
You mocking, changeling, fairy-born and human-bred, you

400
00:26:03,801 --> 00:26:06,770
make me feel as I have not felt these twelve months.

401
00:26:07,970 --> 00:26:11,947
If Saul could have had you for his David, the evil spirit

402
00:26:11,948 --> 00:26:14,591
would have been exercised without the aid of the harp.

403
00:26:15,630 --> 00:26:18,910
There, sir, you are read up and made decent.

404
00:26:19,630 --> 00:26:20,869
Now I'll leave you.

405
00:26:21,389 --> 00:26:24,750
I've been traveling these last three days and I believe I am tired.

406
00:26:25,470 --> 00:26:26,470
Good night.

407
00:26:27,309 --> 00:26:29,089
Just one word, Jane.

408
00:26:30,369 --> 00:26:33,210
Were there only ladies in the house where you have been?

409
00:26:34,190 --> 00:26:39,070
I laughed and made my escape, still laughing as I ran upstairs.

410
00:26:39,949 --> 00:26:42,690
A good idea, I thought with Glee.

411
00:26:43,449 --> 00:26:47,630
I see I have the means of fretting him out of his melancholy for some time to come.

412
00:26:49,910 --> 00:26:53,149
Very early the next morning, I heard him up

413
00:26:53,150 --> 00:26:57,270
and astere, wandering from one room to another.

414
00:26:57,570 --> 00:26:59,830
As soon as Mary came down, I heard the question.

415
00:27:01,029 --> 00:27:02,029
Is Miss Eyre here?

416
00:27:02,729 --> 00:27:03,729
Then?

417
00:27:03,770 --> 00:27:05,289
Which room did you put her into?

418
00:27:05,669 --> 00:27:06,149
Was it dry?

419
00:27:06,490 --> 00:27:07,490
Is she up?

420
00:27:07,669 --> 00:27:10,990
Go and ask if she wants anything and when she will come down.

421
00:27:12,169 --> 00:27:16,570
I came down as soon as I thought there was a prospect of breakfast.

422
00:27:18,009 --> 00:27:23,770
Entering the room very softly, I had a view of him before he discovered my presence.

423
00:27:24,470 --> 00:27:28,163
It was mournful indeed, to witness the subjugation

424
00:27:28,164 --> 00:27:31,809
of that vigorous spirit to a corporeal infirmity.

425
00:27:32,869 --> 00:27:38,089
He sat in this chair, still but not at rest, expectant evidently.

426
00:27:38,830 --> 00:27:42,830
The lines of now habitual sadness marking his strong features.

427
00:27:43,529 --> 00:27:48,630
His countenance reminded one of a lamp quenched, waiting to be relit,

428
00:27:49,149 --> 00:27:55,210
and alas, it was not himself that could now kindle the luster of animated expression.

429
00:27:55,929 --> 00:27:58,929
He was dependent on another for that office.

430
00:28:00,110 --> 00:28:04,089
I had meant to be gay and careless, but the powerlessness

431
00:28:04,091 --> 00:28:06,889
of the strong man touched my heart to the quick.

432
00:28:07,649 --> 00:28:11,889
Still, I accosted him, with what vivacity I could.

433
00:28:12,710 --> 00:28:15,789
It is a bright sunny morning, sir, I said.

434
00:28:16,589 --> 00:28:20,710
The rain is over and gone, and there is a tender shining after it.

435
00:28:21,309 --> 00:28:22,410
You shall have a walk soon.

436
00:28:23,630 --> 00:28:24,990
I had wakened the glow.

437
00:28:25,690 --> 00:28:26,990
His features beamed.

438
00:28:27,710 --> 00:28:30,770
Oh, you are indeed there, my skylock, come to me.

439
00:28:31,630 --> 00:28:33,990
You are not gone, not vanished.

440
00:28:34,750 --> 00:28:38,649
I heard one of your kind an hour ago singing high over the wood.

441
00:28:39,649 --> 00:28:42,110
But its song had no music for me.

442
00:28:42,850 --> 00:28:45,410
Any more than the rising sun had rays.

443
00:28:46,110 --> 00:28:50,910
All the melody on earth is concentrated in my Jane's tongue to my ear.

444
00:28:51,429 --> 00:28:54,029
I'm glad it is not naturally a silent one.

445
00:28:54,470 --> 00:28:57,309
All the sunshine I can feel is in her presence.

446
00:28:59,029 --> 00:29:03,610
The water stood in my eyes to hear this vowl of his dependence.

447
00:29:04,270 --> 00:29:08,338
Just as if a royal eagle chained to a perch should be

448
00:29:08,339 --> 00:29:11,649
forced to entreat a sparrow to become its purveyor.

449
00:29:12,350 --> 00:29:14,190
But I would not be lacrimous.

450
00:29:15,250 --> 00:29:19,490
I dashed off the salt drops and busied myself with preparing breakfast.

451
00:29:20,929 --> 00:29:23,350
Most of the morning was spent in the open air.

452
00:29:24,169 --> 00:29:28,990
I led him out of the wet and wild wood into some cheerful fields.

453
00:29:29,729 --> 00:29:35,250
I described to him how brilliantly green they were, how the flowers and hedges

454
00:29:35,251 --> 00:29:38,949
looked refreshed, how sparklingly blue was the sky.

455
00:29:39,910 --> 00:29:45,289
I sought a seat for him in a hidden and lovely spot, a dry stump of a tree.

456
00:29:46,490 --> 00:29:50,910
Nor did I refuse to let him when seated place me on his knee.

457
00:29:51,910 --> 00:29:55,410
Why should I when both he and I were happier near than a part?

458
00:29:57,070 --> 00:29:59,809
Pilate lay beside us, all was quiet.

459
00:30:00,750 --> 00:30:03,309
He broke out suddenly while clasping me in his arms.

460
00:30:04,630 --> 00:30:06,210
Cruel, cruel deserter.

461
00:30:07,149 --> 00:30:11,309
Oh, Jane, what did I feel when I discovered you had fled from thornfield?

462
00:30:12,250 --> 00:30:14,070
And when I could nowhere find you?

463
00:30:15,070 --> 00:30:21,330
And, after examining your apartment, ascertained that you had taken no money,

464
00:30:22,050 --> 00:30:24,610
nor anything which could serve as an equivalent?

465
00:30:25,929 --> 00:30:30,690
A pearl necklace I had given you, lay untouched in its little casket.

466
00:30:31,490 --> 00:30:33,407
Your trunks were left corded and locked as

467
00:30:33,407 --> 00:30:36,671
they had been prepared for the bridal tour.

468
00:30:36,770 --> 00:30:43,370
What could my darling do, I asked, left destitute and penniless, and what did she do?

469
00:30:44,190 --> 00:30:45,449
Let me hear now.

470
00:30:47,050 --> 00:30:51,750
Thus urged, I began the narrative of my experience for the last year.

471
00:30:52,630 --> 00:30:56,830
I softened considerably what related to the three days of wandering and

472
00:30:56,831 --> 00:31:02,171
starvation, because to have told him all would have been to inflict unnecessary pain.

473
00:31:02,690 --> 00:31:07,589
The little I did say lacerated his faithful heart deeper than I wished.

474
00:31:08,330 --> 00:31:13,309
I should not have left him thus, he said, without any means of making my way.

475
00:31:14,050 --> 00:31:16,210
I should have told him my intention.

476
00:31:16,889 --> 00:31:18,369
I should have confided in him.

477
00:31:18,929 --> 00:31:21,250
He would never have forced me to be his mistress.

478
00:31:22,570 --> 00:31:29,229
Violent as he had seemed in his despair, he, in truth, loved me far too well and

479
00:31:29,230 --> 00:31:32,070
too tenderly to constitute himself my tyrant.

480
00:31:33,229 --> 00:31:37,410
He would have given me half his fortune without demanding so much as a kiss in

481
00:31:37,410 --> 00:31:42,070
return, rather than I should have flung myself friendless on the wide world.

482
00:31:43,050 --> 00:31:45,570
I had endured, he was certain.

483
00:31:46,369 --> 00:31:48,509
More than I had confessed to him.

484
00:31:49,770 --> 00:31:55,169
Well, whatever my sufferings had been, they were very short, I answered.

485
00:31:55,850 --> 00:32:01,130
And then I proceeded to tell him how I had been received at more house, how I had

486
00:32:01,130 --> 00:32:05,809
obtained the office of school mistress, etc., the accession of fortune,

487
00:32:06,110 --> 00:32:09,470
the discovery of my relations, followed in due order.

488
00:32:10,309 --> 00:32:13,990
Of course, engine rivers name came infrequently in the progress of my tale.

489
00:32:14,850 --> 00:32:18,389
When I had done, that name was immediately taken up.

490
00:32:19,850 --> 00:32:22,270
This engine, then, is your cousin?

491
00:32:23,270 --> 00:32:24,270
Yes.

492
00:32:24,750 --> 00:32:26,169
You have spoken of him often.

493
00:32:27,050 --> 00:32:28,050
Do you like him?

494
00:32:28,970 --> 00:32:30,750
He was a very good man, sir.

495
00:32:31,729 --> 00:32:33,229
I could not help liking him.

496
00:32:33,929 --> 00:32:34,929
A good man.

497
00:32:35,330 --> 00:32:38,089
Does that mean a respectable, well -conducted man of 50?

498
00:32:38,850 --> 00:32:39,850
Or what does it mean?

499
00:32:40,869 --> 00:32:42,470
St. Jean was only 29, sir.

500
00:32:43,550 --> 00:32:48,710
Jean-Encore, as the French say, is he a person of low stature,

501
00:32:48,990 --> 00:32:50,130
flagmatic and plain?

502
00:32:50,869 --> 00:32:54,354
A person whose goodness consists rather in his

503
00:32:54,354 --> 00:32:58,389
guiltlessness of vice than in his prowess in virtue.

504
00:32:59,570 --> 00:33:06,270
He is untiringly active, great and exalted deeds are what he lives to perform.

505
00:33:07,309 --> 00:33:08,449
But his brain?

506
00:33:09,330 --> 00:33:11,009
That is probably rather soft.

507
00:33:11,710 --> 00:33:12,710
He means well.

508
00:33:13,169 --> 00:33:15,330
But you shrug your shoulders to hear him talk.

509
00:33:16,589 --> 00:33:17,770
He talks little, sir.

510
00:33:18,490 --> 00:33:20,369
What he does say is ever to the point.

511
00:33:21,089 --> 00:33:22,309
His brain is first rate.

512
00:33:22,830 --> 00:33:24,889
I should think not impressable but vigorous.

513
00:33:26,309 --> 00:33:27,729
Is he an able man, then?

514
00:33:28,789 --> 00:33:29,929
Truly able.

515
00:33:30,949 --> 00:33:32,509
A thoroughly educated man.

516
00:33:33,389 --> 00:33:36,250
Syngin is an accomplished and profound scholar.

517
00:33:37,009 --> 00:33:40,949
His manners, I think, you said are not to your taste?

518
00:33:41,669 --> 00:33:43,350
Priggish and parsonic?

519
00:33:44,149 --> 00:33:48,970
I never mentioned his manners, but unless I had a very bad taste,

520
00:33:49,490 --> 00:33:50,490
they were suited.

521
00:33:50,830 --> 00:33:53,750
They are polished, calm and gentleman -like.

522
00:33:54,929 --> 00:33:59,889
His appearance, I forget what description you gave of his appearance.

523
00:34:00,690 --> 00:34:03,942
A sort of raw, curate, half strangled with his white

524
00:34:03,944 --> 00:34:07,089
neckloth and stilted up on his thick, sold high-loes, eh?

525
00:34:08,690 --> 00:34:09,830
Syngin dresses well.

526
00:34:10,850 --> 00:34:18,190
He's a handsome man, tall, fair, with blue eyes, and a greasy profile, aside.

527
00:34:18,529 --> 00:34:20,210
Damn him, to me.

528
00:34:21,169 --> 00:34:22,229
Did you like him, Jane?

529
00:34:23,449 --> 00:34:26,789
Yes, Mr. Rochester, I liked him, but you asked me that before.

530
00:34:27,889 --> 00:34:30,830
I perceived, of course, the drift of my interlocutor.

531
00:34:31,850 --> 00:34:33,110
Jealousy had got hold of him.

532
00:34:33,550 --> 00:34:36,830
She stung him, but the sting was salutri.

533
00:34:37,550 --> 00:34:40,429
It gave him respite from the gnawing fang of melancholy.

534
00:34:41,309 --> 00:34:44,850
I would not, therefore, immediately charm the snake.

535
00:34:46,490 --> 00:34:50,195
Perhaps you would rather not sit any longer on my knee,

536
00:34:50,197 --> 00:34:53,669
miss air, was the next somewhat unexpected observation.

537
00:34:54,750 --> 00:34:55,970
Why not, Mr. Rochester?

538
00:34:57,589 --> 00:35:03,370
The picture you have just drawn is suggestive of a rather too overwhelming contrast.

539
00:35:04,070 --> 00:35:07,830
Your words have delineated very prettily, a graceful Apollo.

540
00:35:08,669 --> 00:35:15,510
He is present to your imagination, tall, fair, blue-eyed, and with a greasy profile.

541
00:35:16,029 --> 00:35:21,630
Your eyes dwell on a Vulcan, a real blacksmith, brown, broad-shouldered,

542
00:35:21,889 --> 00:35:24,389
and blind, and lame, into the bargain.

543
00:35:25,610 --> 00:35:30,710
I never thought of it before, but you certainly are rather like Vulcan, sir.

544
00:35:31,309 --> 00:35:35,601
Well, you can leave me, ma'am, but before you go,

545
00:35:35,603 --> 00:35:38,610
and he retained me by a firmer grasp than ever.

546
00:35:39,389 --> 00:35:42,389
You will be pleased just to answer me a question or two.

547
00:35:43,669 --> 00:35:44,669
He paused.

548
00:35:45,389 --> 00:35:49,910
What questions, Mr. Rochester, then followed this cross-examination?

549
00:35:51,190 --> 00:35:55,429
Singen made you school mistress of Morton before he knew you were his cousin.

550
00:35:56,289 --> 00:36:01,410
Yes, you would often see him, he would visit the school sometimes?

551
00:36:02,509 --> 00:36:03,509
Daily.

552
00:36:04,110 --> 00:36:05,910
He would approve of your plans, Jane.

553
00:36:06,830 --> 00:36:07,949
I know they would be clever.

554
00:36:08,570 --> 00:36:10,690
For you are a talented creature.

555
00:36:11,669 --> 00:36:13,289
He approved of them, yes.

556
00:36:14,470 --> 00:36:16,350
He would discover many things in you.

557
00:36:16,910 --> 00:36:18,669
He could not have expected to find.

558
00:36:19,910 --> 00:36:21,990
Some of your accomplishments are not ordinary.

559
00:36:23,470 --> 00:36:24,649
I don't know about that.

560
00:36:25,869 --> 00:36:28,050
You had a little cottage near the school, you say.

561
00:36:28,970 --> 00:36:30,330
Did he ever come there to see you?

562
00:36:31,250 --> 00:36:32,250
Now and then.

563
00:36:33,050 --> 00:36:34,050
Of an evening?

564
00:36:34,649 --> 00:36:35,990
Once or twice.

565
00:36:36,850 --> 00:36:37,850
A pause.

566
00:36:39,110 --> 00:36:41,119
How long did you reside with him and his

567
00:36:41,119 --> 00:36:44,051
sisters after the cousin ship was discovered?

568
00:36:44,789 --> 00:36:45,869
Five months.

569
00:36:47,050 --> 00:36:50,029
Did Rivers spend much time with the ladies of his family?

570
00:36:51,009 --> 00:36:55,449
Yes, the back parlour was both his study and ours.

571
00:36:56,089 --> 00:36:58,470
He sat near the window and we by the table.

572
00:36:59,110 --> 00:37:00,470
Did he study much?

573
00:37:01,210 --> 00:37:02,210
A good deal.

574
00:37:02,710 --> 00:37:03,710
What?

575
00:37:03,889 --> 00:37:04,889
Hindostani.

576
00:37:05,169 --> 00:37:07,009
And what did you do mean time?

577
00:37:07,970 --> 00:37:09,570
I learned German at first.

578
00:37:10,509 --> 00:37:11,509
Did he teach you?

579
00:37:11,889 --> 00:37:13,130
He did not understand German.

580
00:37:14,190 --> 00:37:15,190
Did he teach you nothing?

581
00:37:16,050 --> 00:37:17,050
A little Hindostani?

582
00:37:18,029 --> 00:37:19,190
Rivers taught you Hindostani?

583
00:37:19,949 --> 00:37:20,949
Yes, sir.

584
00:37:21,169 --> 00:37:22,169
And his sisters also?

585
00:37:22,889 --> 00:37:25,509
No, only you, only me.

586
00:37:26,149 --> 00:37:27,389
Did you ask to learn?

587
00:37:28,070 --> 00:37:29,070
No.

588
00:37:29,190 --> 00:37:30,190
He wished to teach you?

589
00:37:30,729 --> 00:37:31,729
Yes.

590
00:37:31,809 --> 00:37:32,809
A second pause.

591
00:37:33,250 --> 00:37:34,250
Why did he wish it?

592
00:37:34,750 --> 00:37:36,630
Of what use could Hindostani be to you?

593
00:37:37,889 --> 00:37:39,970
He intended me to go with him to India.

594
00:37:41,990 --> 00:37:44,529
Ah, here I reach the root of the matter.

595
00:37:45,369 --> 00:37:46,470
He wanted you to marry him?

596
00:37:47,210 --> 00:37:48,309
He asked me to marry him.

597
00:37:49,110 --> 00:37:50,610
That is a fiction.

598
00:37:51,309 --> 00:37:52,949
An impudent invention to vex me.

599
00:37:53,690 --> 00:37:54,690
I beg your pardon.

600
00:37:55,470 --> 00:37:56,589
It is the literal truth.

601
00:37:57,570 --> 00:37:59,774
He asked me more than once and was a stiff

602
00:37:59,775 --> 00:38:03,570
about urging his point as ever you could be.

603
00:38:04,229 --> 00:38:06,470
Miss Aya, I repeat it.

604
00:38:06,929 --> 00:38:07,929
You can leave me.

605
00:38:08,690 --> 00:38:10,850
How often am I to say the same thing?

606
00:38:11,970 --> 00:38:15,309
Why do you remain pertinitiously perched on my knee?

607
00:38:15,850 --> 00:38:17,610
When I have given you notice to quit?

608
00:38:18,750 --> 00:38:20,289
Because I am comfortable there.

609
00:38:21,229 --> 00:38:23,750
No, Jane, you are not comfortable there.

610
00:38:24,350 --> 00:38:25,910
Because your heart is not with me.

611
00:38:26,610 --> 00:38:28,910
It is with this cousin, this engine.

612
00:38:30,589 --> 00:38:34,169
Oh, till this moment, I thought my little Jane was all mine.

613
00:38:35,589 --> 00:38:38,990
I had a belief she loved me even when she left me.

614
00:38:39,809 --> 00:38:42,649
That was an atom of sweet in much bitter.

615
00:38:43,850 --> 00:38:49,190
Long as we have been parted, hot tears as I have wept over our separation,

616
00:38:50,029 --> 00:38:53,929
I never thought that while I was mourning her, she was loving another.

617
00:38:55,029 --> 00:38:56,589
But it is useless grieving.

618
00:38:57,830 --> 00:38:58,929
Jane, leave me.

619
00:38:59,570 --> 00:39:00,570
Go and marry Rivers.

620
00:39:02,029 --> 00:39:03,369
Shake me off, then, sir.

621
00:39:03,809 --> 00:39:04,809
Push me away.

622
00:39:04,990 --> 00:39:06,589
For I'll not leave you of my own accord.

623
00:39:08,210 --> 00:39:10,429
Jane, I ever like your tone of voice.

624
00:39:11,149 --> 00:39:12,470
It's still renews hope.

625
00:39:12,929 --> 00:39:13,929
It sounds so truthful.

626
00:39:14,330 --> 00:39:16,570
When I hear it, it carries me back a year.

627
00:39:17,410 --> 00:39:19,369
I forget that you have formed a new tie.

628
00:39:20,050 --> 00:39:21,610
But I am not a fool.

629
00:39:21,949 --> 00:39:22,050
Go.

630
00:39:22,949 --> 00:39:24,250
Where must I go, sir?

631
00:39:25,550 --> 00:39:26,550
Your own way.

632
00:39:26,649 --> 00:39:27,970
With the husband you have chosen.

633
00:39:28,710 --> 00:39:29,710
Who is that?

634
00:39:30,589 --> 00:39:32,330
You know, this engine, Rivers?

635
00:39:33,929 --> 00:39:35,649
He is not my husband.

636
00:39:36,589 --> 00:39:37,710
Nor ever will be.

637
00:39:38,669 --> 00:39:39,789
He does not love me.

638
00:39:40,490 --> 00:39:41,509
I do not love him.

639
00:39:42,529 --> 00:39:44,750
He loves, as he can love.

640
00:39:45,449 --> 00:39:47,070
And that is not as you love.

641
00:39:48,009 --> 00:39:50,350
A beautiful young lady called Rosamond.

642
00:39:50,830 --> 00:39:54,589
He wanted to marry me only because he thought I should make a suitable

643
00:39:54,591 --> 00:39:57,229
missionary's wife, which she would not have done.

644
00:39:58,550 --> 00:40:00,869
He is good and great, but severe.

645
00:40:01,490 --> 00:40:03,770
And for me, cold as an iceberg.

646
00:40:05,149 --> 00:40:06,570
He is not like you, sir.

647
00:40:07,149 --> 00:40:10,649
I am not happy at his side, nor near him, nor with him.

648
00:40:11,509 --> 00:40:14,490
He has no indulgence for me, no fondness.

649
00:40:15,350 --> 00:40:21,111
He sees nothing attractive in me, not even youth, only a few useful mental points.

650
00:40:21,270 --> 00:40:23,509
Then I must leave you, sir, to go to him.

651
00:40:24,809 --> 00:40:27,957
I shuddered involuntarily and clung instinctively

652
00:40:27,959 --> 00:40:30,429
closer to my blind but beloved master.

653
00:40:30,869 --> 00:40:31,869
He smiled.

654
00:40:32,710 --> 00:40:33,710
What, Jane?

655
00:40:34,270 --> 00:40:35,270
Is this true?

656
00:40:35,830 --> 00:40:38,289
Is such really the state of matters between you and Rivers?

657
00:40:39,669 --> 00:40:40,710
Absolutely, sir.

658
00:40:41,589 --> 00:40:43,169
Oh, you need not be jealous.

659
00:40:44,149 --> 00:40:46,449
I wanted to tease you a little to make you less sad.

660
00:40:47,509 --> 00:40:49,330
I thought anger would be better than grief.

661
00:40:50,350 --> 00:40:55,350
But if you wish me to love you, could you but see how much I do love you?

662
00:40:56,029 --> 00:40:57,589
You would be proud and content.

663
00:40:58,369 --> 00:41:00,110
All my heart is yours, sir.

664
00:41:00,750 --> 00:41:04,449
It belongs to you, and with you it would remain, were

665
00:41:04,451 --> 00:41:07,410
fate to exile the rest of me from your presence forever.

666
00:41:08,929 --> 00:41:13,229
Again, as he kissed me, painful thoughts darkened his aspect.

667
00:41:14,350 --> 00:41:17,630
My seared vision, my crippled strength.

668
00:41:18,270 --> 00:41:19,509
He murmured regretfully.

669
00:41:20,369 --> 00:41:22,729
I caressed in order to soothe him.

670
00:41:23,490 --> 00:41:27,589
I knew of what he was thinking and wanted to speak for him but dared not.

671
00:41:28,789 --> 00:41:33,080
As he turned aside his face a minute, I saw a tear slide from

672
00:41:33,081 --> 00:41:37,470
under the sealed eyelid and trickle down the manly cheek.

673
00:41:38,289 --> 00:41:40,169
My heart swelled.

674
00:41:40,970 --> 00:41:47,770
I am no better than the old lightning struck chestnut tree in Thornfield, orchard.

675
00:41:47,949 --> 00:41:48,949
He remarked air long.

676
00:41:50,190 --> 00:41:52,763
And what right would that ruin have to bid a

677
00:41:52,764 --> 00:41:56,191
budding woodbine cover its decay with freshness?

678
00:41:57,470 --> 00:41:59,369
You are no ruin, sir.

679
00:42:00,190 --> 00:42:01,690
No lightning struck tree.

680
00:42:02,369 --> 00:42:03,690
You are green and vigorous.

681
00:42:04,369 --> 00:42:07,165
Plants will grow about your roots, whether you ask them or

682
00:42:07,167 --> 00:42:10,070
not, because they take delight in your bountiful shadow.

683
00:42:10,169 --> 00:42:14,657
And as they grow, they will lean towards you and wind

684
00:42:14,658 --> 00:42:19,149
round you because your strength offers them so safe a prop.

685
00:42:20,050 --> 00:42:21,050
Again, he smiled.

686
00:42:21,429 --> 00:42:22,429
I gave him comfort.

687
00:42:23,369 --> 00:42:24,770
You speak of friends, Jane.

688
00:42:25,509 --> 00:42:26,509
He asked.

689
00:42:27,029 --> 00:42:30,610
Yes, of friends, I answered rather hesitatingly.

690
00:42:31,070 --> 00:42:35,009
For I knew I meant more than friends, but could not tell what other word to employ.

691
00:42:35,610 --> 00:42:36,610
He helped me.

692
00:42:36,770 --> 00:42:39,889
Ah, Jane, but I want a wife.

693
00:42:40,910 --> 00:42:41,910
Do you, sir?

694
00:42:42,729 --> 00:42:44,389
Yes, is it news to you?

695
00:42:45,309 --> 00:42:47,470
Of course, you said nothing about it before.

696
00:42:48,369 --> 00:42:49,809
Is it unwelcome news?

697
00:42:50,649 --> 00:42:53,190
That depends on circumstances, sir, on your choice.

698
00:42:54,490 --> 00:42:55,850
Which you shall make for me, Jane?

699
00:42:56,649 --> 00:42:58,130
I will abide by your decision.

700
00:42:59,070 --> 00:43:00,130
Choose then, sir.

701
00:43:00,869 --> 00:43:01,949
Her who loves you best.

702
00:43:02,710 --> 00:43:03,710
I will at least choose.

703
00:43:04,270 --> 00:43:05,270
Her I love best.

704
00:43:05,610 --> 00:43:06,949
Jane, will you marry me?

705
00:43:07,990 --> 00:43:08,990
Yes, sir.

706
00:43:09,649 --> 00:43:13,330
A poor blind man, whom you will have to lead about by the hand?

707
00:43:14,309 --> 00:43:15,309
Yes, sir.

708
00:43:15,830 --> 00:43:20,350
A crippled man, 20 years older than you, whom you will have to wait on.

709
00:43:21,110 --> 00:43:22,110
Yes, sir.

710
00:43:22,410 --> 00:43:23,410
Truly, Jane?

711
00:43:24,089 --> 00:43:25,089
Most truly, sir.

712
00:43:25,889 --> 00:43:29,270
Oh, my darling, God bless you and reward you.

713
00:43:30,149 --> 00:43:35,710
Mr. Rochester, if ever I did a good deed in my life, if ever I thought a good

714
00:43:35,710 --> 00:43:39,861
thought, if ever I prayed a sincere and blameless prayer,

715
00:43:39,861 --> 00:43:44,490
if ever I wished a righteous wish, I am rewarded now.

716
00:43:45,410 --> 00:43:49,869
To be your wife is for me, to be as happy as I can be on earth.

717
00:43:51,690 --> 00:43:53,550
Because you delight in sacrifice.

718
00:43:55,050 --> 00:43:57,050
Sacrifice, what do I sacrifice?

719
00:43:58,130 --> 00:44:00,750
Famine for food, expectation for content?

720
00:44:01,550 --> 00:44:05,970
To be privileged to put my arms around what I value, to press my lips to what I love?

721
00:44:06,729 --> 00:44:08,410
To repose on what I trust?

722
00:44:09,089 --> 00:44:10,669
Is that to make a sacrifice?

723
00:44:10,671 --> 00:44:15,470
If so, then certainly I delight in sacrifice.

724
00:44:16,610 --> 00:44:21,830
And to bear with my infirmities, Jane, to overlook my deficiencies?

725
00:44:22,630 --> 00:44:24,529
Which are none, sir, to me?

726
00:44:25,250 --> 00:44:29,910
I love you better now when I can really be useful to you than I did in your state of

727
00:44:29,910 --> 00:44:36,391
proud independence when you disdained every part, but that of the giver and protector.

728
00:44:37,389 --> 00:44:41,729
Here the two, I have hated to be helped, to be led.

729
00:44:43,009 --> 00:44:46,009
Henceforth, I feel I shall hate it no more.

730
00:44:47,309 --> 00:44:50,834
I did not like to put my hand into a highlings, but it

731
00:44:50,835 --> 00:44:54,009
is pleasant to feel it circled by Jane's little fingers.

732
00:44:54,830 --> 00:44:59,369
I preferred utter loneliness to the constant attendance of servants,

733
00:45:00,070 --> 00:45:03,529
but Jane's soft ministry will be a perpetual joy.

734
00:45:04,330 --> 00:45:05,330
Jane suits me.

735
00:45:05,869 --> 00:45:06,869
Do I suit her?

736
00:45:08,050 --> 00:45:09,789
To the finest fiber of my nature, sir.

737
00:45:10,949 --> 00:45:14,289
The case being so, we have nothing in the world to wait for.

738
00:45:14,750 --> 00:45:16,509
We must be married instantly.

739
00:45:17,710 --> 00:45:19,529
He looked and spoke with eagerness.

740
00:45:20,250 --> 00:45:22,169
His old impotuosity was rising.

741
00:45:22,949 --> 00:45:25,750
We must become one flesh without any delay, Jane.

742
00:45:26,490 --> 00:45:28,190
There is but the license to get.

743
00:45:29,029 --> 00:45:30,229
Then we marry.

744
00:45:31,550 --> 00:45:37,309
Mr. Rochester, I have just discovered the sun is far declined from its meridian,

745
00:45:38,089 --> 00:45:40,669
and pilot is actually gone home to his dinner.

746
00:45:41,449 --> 00:45:42,509
Let me look at your watch.

747
00:45:44,009 --> 00:45:47,389
Fasten it into your girdle, Janet, and keep it hence forward.

748
00:45:48,050 --> 00:45:49,610
I have no use for it.

749
00:45:51,029 --> 00:45:53,850
It is nearly four o'clock in the afternoon, sir.

750
00:45:54,589 --> 00:45:55,589
Don't you feel hungry?

751
00:45:56,669 --> 00:46:00,190
The third day from this must be our wedding day, Jane.

752
00:46:01,470 --> 00:46:04,149
Never mind fine clothes and jewels now.

753
00:46:05,389 --> 00:46:06,910
All that is not worth a philip.

754
00:46:08,570 --> 00:46:11,470
The sun has dried up all the raindrops, sir.

755
00:46:12,369 --> 00:46:13,410
The breeze is still.

756
00:46:13,710 --> 00:46:14,710
It is quite hot.

757
00:46:16,190 --> 00:46:17,309
Do you know, Jane?

758
00:46:18,309 --> 00:46:20,910
I have your little pearl necklace at this moment.

759
00:46:21,729 --> 00:46:24,850
Fastened round my bronze scrag under my cravat.

760
00:46:25,630 --> 00:46:31,550
I have worn it since the day I lost my only treasure as a memento of her.

761
00:46:32,630 --> 00:46:34,210
We will go home through the wood.

762
00:46:34,910 --> 00:46:36,289
That will be the shadiest way.

763
00:46:37,470 --> 00:46:40,610
He pursued his own thoughts without heeding me.

764
00:46:41,529 --> 00:46:42,529
Jane.

765
00:46:42,869 --> 00:46:46,169
You think me, I dare say, an irreligious dog.

766
00:46:46,869 --> 00:46:51,630
But my heart swells with gratitude to the beneficent god of this earth just now.

767
00:46:52,330 --> 00:46:55,330
He sees not as man sees, but far clearer.

768
00:46:56,070 --> 00:46:59,289
Judges not as man judges, but far more wisely, I did wrong.

769
00:46:59,869 --> 00:47:04,850
I would have solid my innocent flower breathed guilt on its purity.

770
00:47:05,770 --> 00:47:08,169
The omnipotent snatched it from me.

771
00:47:08,809 --> 00:47:13,649
I, in my stiff-necked rebellion, almost cursed the dispensation.

772
00:47:14,330 --> 00:47:17,710
Instead of bending to the decree, I defied it.

773
00:47:18,589 --> 00:47:21,050
Divine justice pursued its course.

774
00:47:21,789 --> 00:47:23,770
Disasters came thick on me.

775
00:47:24,350 --> 00:47:27,130
I was forced to pass through the valley of the shadow of death.

776
00:47:28,050 --> 00:47:32,750
His chastisements are mighty, and once smelt me which has humbled me forever.

777
00:47:34,149 --> 00:47:38,589
You know I was proud of my strength, but what is it now, when I must give it

778
00:47:38,591 --> 00:47:41,949
over to foreign guidance, as a child does its weakness?

779
00:47:43,710 --> 00:47:47,562
Of late Jane only, only of late, I began to

780
00:47:47,562 --> 00:47:51,150
see and acknowledge the hand of god in my doom.

781
00:47:52,070 --> 00:47:58,510
I began to experience remorse, repentance, the wish for reconcilement to my maker.

782
00:47:58,789 --> 00:48:03,869
I began sometimes to pray, very brief prayers they were, but very sincere.

783
00:48:04,929 --> 00:48:08,970
Someday since, nay I can number them, four.

784
00:48:09,789 --> 00:48:13,369
It was last Monday night, a singular mood came over me,

785
00:48:13,370 --> 00:48:17,789
one in which grief replaced frenzy, sorrow, sullenness.

786
00:48:18,570 --> 00:48:20,811
I had long had the impression that since I

787
00:48:20,812 --> 00:48:24,391
could know where find you, you must be dead.

788
00:48:25,330 --> 00:48:30,550
Late that night, perhaps it might be between 11 and 12 o'clock, air I retired

789
00:48:30,551 --> 00:48:37,110
to my dreary rest, I supplicated god that, if it seemed good to him, I might soon be

790
00:48:37,111 --> 00:48:40,589
taken from this life, and admitted to that world to

791
00:48:40,589 --> 00:48:44,110
come, where there was still hope of rejoining Jane.

792
00:48:45,630 --> 00:48:51,850
I was in my own room, and sitting by the window which was open, it soothed me to

793
00:48:51,850 --> 00:48:55,559
feel the barmy night air, though I could see no stars and

794
00:48:55,639 --> 00:49:00,050
only by a vague, luminous haze knew the presence of a moon.

795
00:49:01,029 --> 00:49:02,630
I longed for the Janet.

796
00:49:03,369 --> 00:49:09,289
Oh, I longed for the both with soul and flesh, I asked of god at once in anguish

797
00:49:09,290 --> 00:49:14,410
and humility, if I had not been long enough desolate, afflicted, tormented,

798
00:49:15,050 --> 00:49:18,509
and might not soon taste bliss and peace once more.

799
00:49:19,490 --> 00:49:21,860
That I merited all I endured I acknowledged,

800
00:49:21,861 --> 00:49:24,669
that I could scarcely endure more, I pleaded.

801
00:49:25,589 --> 00:49:28,706
And the alpha and omega of my heart's wishes broke

802
00:49:28,706 --> 00:49:33,669
involuntarily from my lips in the words Jane, Jane, Jane.

803
00:49:34,690 --> 00:49:36,570
Did you speak these words aloud?

804
00:49:37,589 --> 00:49:38,589
I did, Jane.

805
00:49:39,330 --> 00:49:42,250
If any listener had heard me, he would have thought

806
00:49:42,251 --> 00:49:45,330
me mad, I pronounced them with such frantic energy.

807
00:49:46,490 --> 00:49:49,630
And it was last Monday night, somewhere near midnight?

808
00:49:50,610 --> 00:49:53,389
Yes, but the time is of no consequence.

809
00:49:54,389 --> 00:49:56,550
What followed is the strange point.

810
00:49:57,429 --> 00:50:02,230
You will think me superstitious, some superstition I have in my blood and always had.

811
00:50:02,570 --> 00:50:04,610
Nevertheless, this is true.

812
00:50:05,429 --> 00:50:08,429
True at least it is that I heard what I now relate.

813
00:50:10,089 --> 00:50:15,630
As I exclaimed, Jane, Jane, Jane, a voice, I cannot tell whence the voice

814
00:50:15,630 --> 00:50:20,929
came, but I know whose voice it was, replied, I am coming, wait for me,

815
00:50:21,570 --> 00:50:26,649
and a moment after, went whispering on the wind the words, where are you?

816
00:50:27,850 --> 00:50:33,570
I'll tell you if I can, the idea the picture, these words open to my mind.

817
00:50:34,130 --> 00:50:36,990
Yet it is difficult to express what I want to express.

818
00:50:37,710 --> 00:50:41,213
Ferndian is buried, as you see, in a heavy wood,

819
00:50:41,214 --> 00:50:44,770
where sound falls dull and dies unreverberating.

820
00:50:45,630 --> 00:50:46,630
Where are you?

821
00:50:47,169 --> 00:50:53,270
Seemed spoken amongst mountains, for I heard a hill-sent echo repeat the words.

822
00:50:53,850 --> 00:50:57,270
Cooler and fresher at the moment the gale seemed to visit my brow.

823
00:50:58,110 --> 00:51:03,589
I could have deemed that in some wild, lone scene, I and Jane were meeting.

824
00:51:04,550 --> 00:51:06,570
In spirit, I believe we must have met.

825
00:51:07,050 --> 00:51:09,990
You know doubt were at that hour in unconscious sleep, Jane.

826
00:51:11,210 --> 00:51:14,070
Perhaps your soul wandered from itself to comfort mine.

827
00:51:14,850 --> 00:51:19,869
For those were your accents, as certain as I live, they were yours.

828
00:51:21,309 --> 00:51:24,688
Reader, it was on Monday night, near midnight,

829
00:51:24,690 --> 00:51:27,830
that I too had received the mysterious summons.

830
00:51:28,369 --> 00:51:31,410
Those were the very words by which I replied to it.

831
00:51:32,050 --> 00:51:37,089
I listened to Mr. Rochester's narrative, but made no disclosure in return.

832
00:51:37,990 --> 00:51:40,775
The coincidence struck me as too awful and

833
00:51:40,777 --> 00:51:44,230
inexplicable to be communicated or discussed.

834
00:51:44,630 --> 00:51:49,225
If I told anything, my tale would be such, as must necessarily

835
00:51:49,225 --> 00:51:53,149
make a profound impression, on the mind of my hero.

836
00:51:53,889 --> 00:51:57,774
And that mind, yet from its sufferings too prone to

837
00:51:57,774 --> 00:52:01,250
gloom, needed not the deeper shade of the supernatural.

838
00:52:01,929 --> 00:52:05,729
I kept these things then and pondered them in my heart.

839
00:52:07,589 --> 00:52:13,369
You cannot now wonder, continued my master, that when you rose upon me so

840
00:52:13,370 --> 00:52:18,410
unexpectedly last night, I had difficulty in believing you any other than a mere

841
00:52:18,410 --> 00:52:23,570
voice and vision, something that would melt to silence and annihilation,

842
00:52:24,210 --> 00:52:28,089
as the midnight whisper and mountain echo had melted before.

843
00:52:28,850 --> 00:52:30,509
Now I thank God.

844
00:52:31,330 --> 00:52:32,610
I know it to be otherwise.

845
00:52:33,470 --> 00:52:34,809
Yes, I thank God.

846
00:52:35,929 --> 00:52:41,990
He put me off his knee, rose, and reverently lifting his hat from his brow

847
00:52:41,990 --> 00:52:44,910
and bending his sightless eyes to the earth.

848
00:52:45,630 --> 00:52:47,369
He stood in mute devotion.

849
00:52:48,550 --> 00:52:51,070
Only the last words of the worship were audible.

850
00:52:52,490 --> 00:52:57,770
I thank my maker, that in the midst of judgment he has remembered mercy.

851
00:52:59,410 --> 00:53:02,513
I humbly entreat my Redeemer to give me strength to

852
00:53:02,514 --> 00:53:06,029
lead henceforth a pure life than I have done hither to.

853
00:53:06,910 --> 00:53:08,910
Then he stretched his hand out to be led.

854
00:53:09,630 --> 00:53:12,714
I took that dear hand, held it a moment to

855
00:53:12,716 --> 00:53:16,490
my lips, then led it pass around my shoulder.

856
00:53:16,729 --> 00:53:22,190
Being so much lower of stature than he, I served both for his prop and guide.

857
00:53:23,389 --> 00:53:26,169
We entered the wood and wedded homeward.
